surface-arclength-reference-classic.out
Ordinary arc length continues to scale external reference loads by its load level
StaticStructural solverType "calm" nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 stepLength 0.02 Psi 0. hpc 2 2 1 MaxIter 30 rtolv 1.e-11 rtolf 1.e-11 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 2dPlaneStress
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all
ndofman 2 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 3 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 3
# A unit membrane with mu=1 and no surface tension has axial force P=s-1/s, s=1+u_right.
# The unit reference force on the free right end is multiplied by Lambda. HPC selects u_right=0.02,
# hence Lambda=1.02-1/1.02=0.03960784313725496, and the fixed-end reaction is -Lambda.
node 1 coords 2 0 0
node 2 coords 2 1 0
lineplanestrainsurface 1 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
surfacetensionmat 1 mu 1 d 1
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0 set 2
NodalLoad 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 1.0 set 3 reference
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1
Set 1 nodes 1 1
Set 2 nodes 2 1 2
Set 3 nodes 1 2
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-9
#NODE tStep 1 number 2 dof 1 unknown d value 0.02
#NODE tStep 1 number 2 dof 2 unknown d value 0.0
#LOADLEVEL tStep 1 value 0.03960784313725496
#REACTION tStep 1 number 1 dof 1 value -0.03960784313725496
#%END_CHECK%
